== 6. Nesting: pooled level = same J with stake W = sum w_i B_i^2; level-by-level solving vs the joint optimum
closure: J*(nW) = n^(1/alpha) J*(W); pooled/separate = n^(a-1) with a = 1/alpha; pooled read interval shrinks as n^(-1/alpha)  (verified)
kappa, relative regret of level-by-level solving:
  kappa=0.0: 2.220e-16
  kappa=0.05: 1.889e-05
  kappa=0.1: 7.378e-05
  kappa=0.2: 2.819e-04
  kappa=0.4: 1.035e-03
  kappa=0.8: 3.564e-03
log-log slope of the regret at small kappa: 1.95 (second order: 2)
stake-passing coupling (pooled stake, the case in the theory): sequential = joint exactly; feedback that changes a lower layer's own error: regret O(kappa^2)

